# Docker Rules

## Multi-stage Dockerfile
Build with a JDK image, run with a JRE image. The runtime image must not contain Maven or the JDK.

```dockerfile
# build stage
FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17 AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY pom.xml .
RUN mvn -q -B dependency:go-offline
COPY src ./src
RUN mvn -q -B -DskipTests package

# runtime stage
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre-alpine
WORKDIR /app
RUN addgroup -S app && adduser -S app -G app
USER app
COPY --from=build /app/target/*.jar app.jar
EXPOSE 8080
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --retries=3 \
    CMD wget -qO- http://localhost:8080/actuator/health | grep -q '"status":"UP"' || exit 1
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "/app/app.jar"]
```

## docker-compose
- App + `postgres:16-alpine`. Postgres exposes 5432 to the app only (no host port in prod compose).
- App `depends_on: { postgres: { condition: service_healthy } }`.
- Volumes: a named volume for Postgres data. Never bind-mount onto the running Postgres data dir.
- Health checks on both services. The app's health check hits `/actuator/health`.

## Image Hygiene
- Run as a non-root user (`app`).
- Pin base image tags (`eclipse-temurin:17-jre-alpine`, `postgres:16-alpine`).
- `.dockerignore` excludes `target/`, `.git/`, `.idea/`, `*.iml`.

## Env Vars
- `SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=docker` in the compose file.
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://postgres:5432/blog`
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME` / `SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD` from a `.env` (gitignored).
